 ```

+#### signal
+
+Type: [`AbortSignal`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal)
+
+Cancel queued (not yet started) tasks when the signal aborts. This is equivalent to calling `clearQueue()` when the signal fires, and also discards any task queued afterwards. Already-running tasks are not affected.
+
+Combine with `rejectOnClear` to reject discarded tasks with the signal's abort reason instead of leaving them unresolved.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 1, rejectOnClear: true, signal: controller.signal});
+
+// Later, for example on shutdown
+controller.abort();
+```
+
 ### limit(fn, ...args)

 Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`.
